'''L0-LA59''',<ref name="Part III" /> nicknamed "'''Lola'''," was a [[Gender|feminine]]<ref name="Part I" /> [[L0 droid|L0]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> [[toy droid]]<ref name="Part I AD" /> owned by the [[House of Organa]] and was in the personal possession of the [[Youngling|young]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia]] of [[Alderaan]] during the [[Imperial Era]]. She was built with [[Color|white]] and red plates on the top half of her, and [[silver]] plates on the bottom. She also had small pairs of wings, [[Limb|legs]], [[photoreceptor]]s, and an [[antenna]] near her back. Finally on her inside was a compartment to store miniature tools.

In [[9 BBY]], she would accompany Organa when she was [[Ambush on Alderaan|kidnapped]] by [[Vect Nokru]]'s [[Black Mask|crew]] sent by the [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]] to lure out the secluded [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]. While her master was taken from [[planet]] to planet, she protected her together with the old [[Jedi]], but was given a [[restraining bolt]] by Reva, which briefly worked to foil [[Hunt for Obi-Wan|their escape]]. Once it was removed, she became an accomplice of the [[Hidden Path]] and brought hope to all who traveled it. She and her friends were eventually able to get Organa [[Homeworld|home]]. Safe and far away from the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Inquisitorius]], and [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].

Years after their adventure, in [[1 BBY]], the Galactic Empire had finished the construction of their [[superweapon]], the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. When [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin|Tarkin]] interrogated Organa about where the hidden base of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] was, he ordered the test-firing of the weapon on Alderaan. Lola was destroyed during [[Destruction of Alderaan|the Disaster]], along with millions of other [[Alderaanian]]s, including the rest of Organa's family and friends.

==Biography==
{{Quote|No Lola for the rest of the day.''"<br />"''But she didn't do anything.''"<br />"''Shut her down. I mean it.|Breha and Leia Organa, after Leia ran away.|<ref name="Part I" />}}
[[File:LeiaLOLA-CGSWG.png|thumb|220px|left|Lola was small enough to fit in young Leia Organa's hand.]]
Lola, who was owned by the [[Youngling|young]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] during the [[Imperial Era]], would usually accompany her owner when she played in the royal courts of the [[Royal Palace of Alderaan|Palace]] of [[Alderaan]]. One [[Standard day|day]]<ref name="Part I" /> in [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> the [[mercenary]] [[Vect Nokru]] snuck into the yard and he along with [[Black Mask|his crew]] were able to [[Ambush on Alderaan|kidnap]] the princess, playing under the order of the [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]]. In their [[starship]], Lola attempted to cut the [[rope]]s Organa was tied with using her [[Circular saw|buzz saw]], but Nokru saw the scheme they had concocted and temporarily destroyed Lola. Meanwhile, Organa's [[Parent|father]], [[Bail Prestor Organa]], asked the secluded [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] to go and rescue her. After some convincing, he agreed, and went to dig out his [[lightsaber]] he had buried in the [[desert]] years ago.<ref name="Part I" />

On the [[planet]] [[Daiyu]], Organa grabbed Lola out of her pocket once she and Kenobi had a chance to rest in an alleyway. He demanded that no sound would come from the [[droid]], but Organa assured that none would be made from the broken machine. Once the two reached the destination that would presumably lead them to safety, provided by [[Haja Estree]], they had a [[Search for Princess Leia|skirmish]] with the Third Sister who was interrupted by [[the Grand Inquisitor]], and he indirectly allowed them to escape through a [[TR-286 transport|TR-286]] automated transport, leading to the planet [[Mapuzo]].<ref name="Part II" />

On the [[Transport eight|transport]], Kenobi was able to calm himself down, despite the dire circumstance, and fix Lola. He handed the toy to Organa, who would keep it on her until they reached a [[Mapuzo mining village]], where she presented Lola to the [[loader droid]] [[NED-B]], telling her to greet him.<ref name="Part III" />

[[File:ObiWanKenobi4-variantart-Stott.jpg|thumb|right|250px|L0-LA59 was turned into a puppet of the Empire against her will.]]
In the [[Fortress Inquisitorius]], on the [[ocean]] [[moon]] of [[Nur]], Organa attempted to use Lola to help her [[Rescue of Princess Leia (9 BBY)|escape]] an [[Torture|interrogation]] by the Third Sister, but the droid was noticed by the [[Inquisitor]], and was [[Telekinesis|Force pulled]] to her. Unbeknownst to Organa, Lola was given a [[Homing beacon|tracker]] and subsequently developed [[Color|red]] [[sensor]]s and a rude personality. The Third Sister shared the prior information with [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], after Organa's escape, and they used Lola to follow the fugitives of the [[Hidden Path]] to their base on [[Jabiim]].<ref name="Part IV" />

Once arriving on Jabiim, the reprogrammed Lola flew into the base's power plant and hacked into the electrical systems to seal the [[hangar]] roof. Organa participated to fix the systems herself so the trapped innocents could [[Attack on Jabiim|escape]], and inside the vents she encountered Lola, who attacked her with the same [[arc welder]] used to ruin the systems. Organa was able to suspend her and remove the [[restraining bolt]] from her back, and Lola's [[photoreceptor]]s turned blue again, her malicious programming removed, and she assisted Organa in fixing the hangar doors before their escape.<ref name="Part V" />

In the [[Realspace|space]] above Jabiim, the [[transport]] the innocents were taking came under attack by [[Darth]] Vader's [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyer]], ''[[Devastator]].'' As [[Kawlan Roken's second freight transport|The Path's ship]] was being fired upon, the people inside began to grow worried of their own [[Death|survival]]. Organa brought out Lola to distract the people of the dire circumstance, and specifically focused on the [[Force-sensitive]] boy [[Corran]], and his [[Parent|mother]],<ref name="Part VI">{{Kenobi|Part VI}}</ref> [[Nyche]].<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> As Organa told Kenobi about the hope the two were spreading, Kenobi said that he could use a friend like Lola, and gave Organa the [[holster]] of [[Tala Durith]]. This inspired Organa to stow Lola on the [[dropship]] Kenobi would later tell he had to take, for the survival of everyone onboard. Darth Vader focused all the Devastator's attention on the ship, which made its way to a [[Unidentified barren moon|barren moon]]. Once the Jedi Master landed he noticed the symbol Organa left behind for him, and Lola cheered Kenobi on as he [[Fight on a barren moon|dueled]] his old [[Padawan]]. Organa eventually returned to Alderaan, where she would wait for her friend to return. And eventually he did, and gave Lola back to Organa, in which she would store her in Tala's holster. Organa and Lola then said goodbye to their new friend.<ref name="Part VI" />

In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Alderaan date" /> Lola was destroyed during [[Destruction of Alderaan|the Disaster]] along with everyone else on Alderaan. Years later, after having become engaged to [[Corellian]] [[Han Solo]], the now grown up Leia remembered Lola when she thought of the small things she'd lost due to Alderaan's destruction.<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel">''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]''</ref>

==Equipment==
===Toy droid===
Lola, being a toy droid, had incredibly small height, depth, and width. She was small enough to fit into a pocket, holster, or even the palm of a child's [[Limb|hand]]. This size could be used to fly into tight spaces and fix&mdash;or ruin&mdash;cables and devices of the like. The plating on the top of her shell was red and white, where in the front she had [[Eye|two blue sensors]] with a pupil in the middle of the biggest. Lola was also built with two small wings on the sides that served no actual purpose in flying. But in the center of this half was an off button, and near the end an [[antenna]]. The bottom side of Lola was plated [[silver]], where she had two small, retractable legs that she used when perching. Lola possessed the ability to float in the air, due to a set of small wings, and could travel fast enough to keep up with a running child.

===Accessories===
Inside the bottom half of Lola was a small compartment that stored a variety of tools, some of which were a buzz saw,<ref name="Part I" /> [[glowrod]],<ref name="Part III" /> and an arc welder.<ref name="Part V" /> All of these tools would be used to help Organa during her venture following The Path and escaping the Empire in 9 BBY.<ref name="Date" /> Although the arc welder was used as a weapon against Organa while Lola was reprogrammed.<ref name="Part V" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|[Deborah Chow] didn't even pitch the entire show to me, but just said, 'There's a little girl and she's going to have this droid that's like a toy or companion. This would be the baby version of R2-D2.|Jon Borland|<ref name="Saga chronicles">{{SW|url=news/saga-chronicles-obi-wan-kenobi-sound|text=Saga Chronicles: Skywalker Sound's Danielle Dupre and Jon Borland on Their ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' Journey}}</ref>}}
Lola was first pictured in a [[Wikipedia:Volkswagen|Volkswagen]] commercial that showcased the ID. Buzz,<ref name="Commercial">{{OfficialYouTube|channel=@vw|name=Volkswagen USA|video=6QVKyhFBR3g|text=ID. Buzz is simply galactic - Streaming Now}}</ref> a car that was made in collaboration with [[Lucasfilm]] to promote the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series.<ref name="Volkswagen">{{SW|url=news/obi-wan-kenobi-volkswagen|text=The Story Behind Lucasfilm and Volkswagen's Fantastic ''Obi-Wan Kenobi''-Inspired Vehicles}}</ref> She first appeared in the [[Part I|first episode]] of the series, which was released on [[May 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="Episode 1 Premiere">{{Twitter|obiwankenobi|status/1530019678562549760|''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''|quote=The time for #ObiWanKenobi has arrived&hellip;early. Start streaming the first two episodes on @DisneyPlus TONIGHT at 9PM PT.|archivedate=20220527053945}}</ref> She was first identified as L0-LA59 in a [[StarWars.com]] article announcing Lola products that were revealed at [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|Celebation Anaheim]], 2022.<ref name="Products">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-hasbro-star-wars-panel|text=SWCA 2022: 7 Hasbro ''Star Wars'' Reveals Fans Won't Want to Miss}}</ref>

The sound of Lola was created by sound designer and editor [[Jon Borland]]. During his earliest work on the series, director [[Deborah Chow]] consulted with him about the concept of a little girl having a droid companion that would be the baby version of [[R2-D2]]. The final sound for Lola included pieces of Borland's voice and his daughter saying "[[May the Force be with you]]." He manipulated the voices to sound like beeps and boops. Borland was inspired by how sound designer [[Ben Burtt]] used his own voice for R2-D2.<ref name="Saga chronicles" /> The propmakers were assigned with designing a holster that could fit young Leia Organa and the adult Tala Durith. Propmaster [[Brad Elliott]] found this to be challenging because of the actors' height differences and it had to hold Lola and Durith's [[blaster]]. To fill the space needed to accommodate Lola, a [[Han Solo]]-style [[scope]] was added to Durith's blaster.<ref name="Brewing rebellion">{{SW|url=news/inside-the-lucasfilm-archive-obi-wan-kenobi-props-3|text=Inside the Lucasfilm Archive: A Brewing Rebellion in the ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' Limited Series}}</ref> [[Doug Chiang]] described Lola as "Leia's [[Wikipedia:Jiminy Cricket|Jiminy Cricket]]."<ref name="Designing the Galaxy">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=Designing the Galaxy}}</ref> Lola's design is reminiscent of early designs of the head of [[BD-1]] done for the [[2019]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order]]'' by [[Jordan Lamarre-Wan]].<ref name="ArtofJFO">''[[The Art of Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order]]''</ref>

